      "writtenOn": "2024-03-25T18:31:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "True, but \"someMax\" changes when the size of the fuzz corpus changes...\n\nMy concern here is that ConsumeIntegralInRange reads a variable number of bytes depending on the range between the min and max.  If it reads more bytes, that will offset all the following data that\u0027s read by the fuzzer, which may make it harder for the fuzzer to adapt (eg. if all it did was add a single byte, and everything being fed through the APIs changed).\n\nIt\u0027d be rare (it\u0027d only happen if the range grows or shrinks past what can be represented in the same number of bytes), so if there isn\u0027t a reasonable Max value that we can use here, this is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "3b72b8b3_9dc92281",
      "revId": "34c2458929efcbaf41affa77251058834454260e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
